# Print-in-place fit proof: the wheel must be a free captive body, clearing the
# fixed base + post + cap + both pawl blocks and both pawls on every surface.
# `fitcheck` renders wheel ∩ fixed and must be EMPTY (bore radial gap, axial
# base/cone gaps, tooth-tip-to-block web_clr, and the pawl's static clearances
# — nose face lock_gap from the tooth wall, beam web_clr over the tips, hook
# clear of the ramp — all clear in the as-drawn pose). `fitcheck_neg` shrinks
# the bore onto the post so it MUST overlap, proving the check can fail.
fitcheck      empty
fitcheck_neg  interferes
